Requirements: 33   with obligations: 32   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] When the stage that prescribes tests returns no prescription for a criterion
    it was asked about, the review still completes and reports that criterion's
    prescription as one that was not obtained.
    -> omitted-criterion-recorded-as-not-obtained  [functional/explicit]   (also serves completion-04)
       The omitted criterion is present in the persisted review state as a prescription
       that was not obtained.

[constraint-01] A response that omits one or more of the criteria the prescribing stage
    was asked about does not end the review.
    -> response-omission-does-not-end-review  [functional/explicit]
       A response that omits one or more of the criteria the prescribing stage was asked
       about does not end the review.

[constraint-02] A review whose prescribing stage omitted a criterion still produces a
    report and a verdict.
    -> omitted-criterion-review-still-produces-report-and-verdict  [functional/explicit]
       A review whose prescribing stage omitted a criterion still produces a report and
       a verdict.

[constraint-03] The prescriptions returned for the other criteria in that same response
    are kept.
    -> other-prescriptions-are-kept  [invariant/explicit]
       The prescriptions returned for the other criteria in that same response are kept.

[constraint-04] Every criterion the prescribing stage was asked about is present in the
    persisted review state, either with a prescribed test or as a prescription that was
    not obtained.
    -> persist-omitted-criterion-state  [functional/explicit]
       Persist every criterion the prescribing stage was asked about, representing each
       one either with a prescribed test or as a prescription that was not obtained.

[constraint-05] A criterion whose prescription was not obtained is distinguishable in
    the persisted review state from a criterion carrying a prescribed test.
    -> not-obtained-distinct-from-prescribed-test  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves completion-05)
       A prescription that was not obtained is distinguishable in the persisted review
       state from a prescribed test.

[constraint-06] A criterion whose prescription was not obtained is distinguishable from
    a criterion that is owed no test.
    -> distinguish-not-obtained-from-no-test  [invariant/explicit]
       Represent a criterion whose prescription was not obtained distinctly from a
       criterion that is owed no test.

[constraint-07] The report states, for a criterion whose prescription was not obtained,
    that no prescription was produced for it.
    -> report-no-prescription-produced  [functional/explicit]
       State in the report, for a criterion whose prescription was not obtained, that no
       prescription was produced for it.
    -> report-says-no-prescription-produced  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       The report states, for a criterion whose prescription was not obtained, that no
       prescription was produced for it.

[constraint-08] The report renders that differently from a criterion that is owed no
    test.
    -> report-renders-not-obtained-differently-from-no-test  [explanation_observability/explicit]   (also serves completion-08)
       The report renders that differently from a criterion that is owed no test.

[constraint-09] A criterion whose prescription was not obtained is not rated as strongly
    supported on the test-evidence axis.
    -> not-obtained-not-strongly-supported  [invariant/explicit]
       Rate a criterion whose prescription was not obtained as not strongly supported on
       the test-evidence axis.

[constraint-10] A review containing a criterion whose prescription was not obtained does
    not conclude that no material gaps remain.
    -> not-obtained-does-not-close-gaps  [regression/explicit]
       Keep a review containing a criterion whose prescription was not obtained from
       concluding that no material gaps remain.

[constraint-11] A response naming a criterion the prescribing stage did not ask about is
    rejected.
    -> reject-unasked-criterion  [error_handling/explicit]
       Reject a response that names a criterion the prescribing stage did not ask about.

[constraint-12] A response naming the same criterion more than once is rejected.
    -> reject-duplicate-criterion-names  [error_handling/explicit]
       Reject a response that names the same criterion more than once.
    -> duplicate-criterion-rejected  [error_handling/explicit]
       A response naming the same criterion more than once is rejected.

[constraint-13] Two runs over the same mandate and the same model responses produce the
    same report.
    -> deterministic-report-for-same-inputs  [regression/explicit]
       Produce the same report for two runs over the same mandate and the same model
       responses.

[exclusion-01] Whether the stage asks the model again for the criteria it omitted.
    -> no-reasking-for-omitted-criteria  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter whether the stage asks the model again for the criteria
       it omitted.

[exclusion-02] How many criteria are carried in one request to the model.
    -> no-change-to-criteria-per-request  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter how many criteria are carried in one request to the
       model.

[exclusion-03] Why the model omits a criterion.
    -> no-omission-cause-analysis  [human_review/explicit]
       The change does not add reasoning about why the model omits a criterion.

[exclusion-04] Which criteria are owed a test at all.
    -> no-change-to-test-owed-criteria-selection  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter which criteria are owed a test at all.

[exclusion-05] How a criterion's existing test evidence is rated.
    -> no-change-to-existing-test-evidence-rating  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter how a criterion's existing test evidence is rated.

[exclusion-06] What the other stages do when their own responses omit a criterion.
    -> no-change-to-other-stage-omission-handling  [regression/explicit]
       The change does not alter what the other stages do when their own responses omit
       a criterion.

